Z||000000||TylerB11||07-09-2001||10:25 AM||||After changing the the oil/filter, plugs, wires, cap, and air filter, my idle has come down some. The soft 1/4" line from the hard line to the EGR was rotted out, so I replaced that, and the warm idle is now at like 1200 RPMs. <BR>But now while at idle, I notice a clicking sound every ten seconds or so. It goes "click" then the idle jumps to 1800RPMs..then settles back down...then "Click" and it jumps again.<BR>The click is definitely in the engine compartment.<P>Anyone ever hear of this before?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierochic88||07-09-2001||11:12 AM||||Could be an AC Compressor...mine clicked when it was bad...<P>Jennifer<P>------------------<BR>IM Username:  FieroChic88<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/jenscar-sig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||TylerB11||07-09-2001||11:27 AM||||Hmm...thats the one thing I didn't think it was...the thing makes freakin ice cubes..||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||07-09-2001||12:35 PM||||The ECM controls idle speed.  When the A/C calls for the compressor clutch to engage the ECM hits the throttle a bit 1/2 second before it engages the clutch.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||07-09-2001||07:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierochic88:<BR><B>Could be an AC Compressor...mine clicked when it was bad...<P>Jennifer<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>the AC clutch always click when they engage. it will click on and off during operation too. it doesnt stay engaged all the time except when its on MAX/RECIR.<P>||||reg||1
